<resources>
    <!--
      Network behaviour of the Discover feed (SPECS.md §5.1 and §5.2). A file of
      its own rather than part of `strings.xml`: Android merges the resources of
      a single folder, and keeping this batch separate avoids making several
      pieces of work converge on one file.
    -->

    <!--
      Offline banner. Neither “error” nor “failure”: SPECS.md §5.2 asks for the
      state to be signalled “without being alarming”, and what the user has in
      front of them works — these are their articles, simply not the most recent
      ones. The message therefore says what they are reading, not what is
      missing.
    -->
    <string name="discover_offline_banner">Offline · you are reading the articles already saved</string>

    <!--
      Opening refused for lack of network (SPECS.md §5.2). Explicit about the
      cause **and** about what was done: opening the custom tab would only have
      shown the browser's error page, without saying why.
    -->
    <string name="discover_offline_open_blocked">Without a connection, this article cannot be opened. It stays in your feed.</string>
    <string name="discover_offline_notice_dismiss">Dismiss</string>
</resources>
